 status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>56121601</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6024701-U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6024701</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6182322-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6182322</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1120166A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMOE KOGYO KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANO SAIHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOE ENGINEERING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, SAIHEI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, TAKAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANO SAIHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANO, SAIHEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of washing a rotating tube of a horizontal type tubular centrifugal separator capable of removing, to the outside of the rotating tube, precipitate deposited on the inner wall of the tube of the horizontal type tubular centrifugal separator rotating with both ends thereof supported on bearings, comprising the steps of charging a plurality of solids for washing into the rotating tube, feeding washing fluid into the rotating tube, rotating the rotating tube, and draining the precipitation together with the washing fluid, the solids for washing being charged into the rotating tube before centrifugal separation or charged into the rotating tube at the time of washing after the centrifugal separation, whereby the manual precipitation removal of a conventional centrifugal separator has been eliminated to reduce a washing cost, and an independent use of a large-sized centrifugal separator which was difficult in the conventional centrifugal separator has been enabled.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de lavage d'un tube tournant de séparateur centrifuge tubulaire de type horizontal capable d'évacuer vers l'extérieur du tube tournant, le précipité déposé sur la paroi intérieure du tube du séparateur centrifuge tubulaire de type horizontal tournant, alors que ses deux extrémités reposent sur des paliers. Ledit procédé consiste à charger plusieurs solides de lavage dans le tube tournant, à envoyer du fluide de lavage dans le tube tournant, à faire tourner le tube tournant et à évacuer le précipité conjointement avec le fluide de lavage. Les solides pour le lavage sont chargés dans le tube tournant avant la séparation centrifuge, ou sont chargés dans le tube tournant au moment du lavage, après la séparation centrifuge. Ainsi, le retrait manuel du précipité d'un séparateur centrifuge classique est supprimé, ce qui permet de réduire le coût du lavage et d'utiliser un séparateur centrifuge de grande taille, ce qui était difficile avec les séparateurs centrifuges classiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>